{"id":"dadb2dc0-74fb-4220-bcc2-5ca0a4797f0e","object":"chat.completion","created":1793258801,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Reading `logger.py` imports and the start of the config class before editing.\n\n```python\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", 1, 32)['content'])\nprint('=====ENVIRON 95-132=====')\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", 95, 132)['content'])\n```","reasoning_content":"I have the key evidence. I need to see the environ.py refresh functions (rearm/rearm_all) — got them. Also need where envs class starts to place new config under Logging. Let me now make edits.\n\nFor environ.py: add a helper factory? The task says descriptor class can add auxiliary factory method. I can use `EnvVar(lambda v: ...)` with validation. Need: None if unset, int parse, >=32, else ValueError including var name. Descriptor wraps error with `f\"{self.name}: {e}\"` so variable name included automatically. But careful: for unset returns None.\n\nAdd under `# -- Logging --`:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(lambda v: None if v is None else _log_max_message_chars(v))\n```\nNeed `_log_max_message_chars` helper defined at module level before class. Let's add:\n\n```python\ndef _positive_int_at_least_32(v: str) -> int:\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{v!r}, must be >= 32\")\n    return value\n```\nHmm, empty string -> int('') raises ValueError(\"invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\") -> wrapped with name. Good.\n\nActually I could add a factory method `EnvVar.int_or_none_at_least(minimum)` but simpler module helper. But task says \"可增加必要标准库辅助函数\" — allowed.\n\nFor logger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with keyword-only max_message_chars. Truncate after `super().format(record)` but need only message body, not prefixes. Approach: in format(), before calling super, handle record.message? Better: compute msg via super().format(record) but we need to truncate only the body. We can construct: temporarily... cannot modify shared record msg/args. We can compute the formatted message ourselves by using `record.getMessage()`, then truncate, then build prefix.\n\nSimplest: after `msg = super().format(record)`, `record.message` is set by super().format (logging.Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage()). Actually the base Formatter.format sets record.message. Then msg contains prefix + message + exception text. We can truncate by replacing the occurrence of record.message in msg at the right position. But careful: record.message may appear elsewhere. Use index: `msg.find(record.message)` — that's what original code does for prefix. But exception text appended after. So:\n\n```python\nif self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n    body = record.message\n    if len(body) > max:\n        truncated = ...\n        # replace the body inside msg\n```\nDoing replacement in msg: find body start = msg.find(body). Then msg = msg[:start] + truncated + msg[start+len(body):]. But if the body occurs in the timestamp? Unlikely.\n\nBut the check \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" — record.getMessage() does that. Good.\n\nHowever better approach: override format to compute message first and set record.message? We must not modify record.msg/args; record.message is set by base anyway and is newly set. Hmm, setting record.message is done by base Formatter; keeping full message is important for subsequent handlers — other handlers call format again and base sets record.message = record.getMessage() fresh, so fine.\n\nBut safer: avoid relying on record.message attribute in msg; compute formatted body ourselves:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        body = record.message\n        if len(body) > self.max_message_chars:\n            ...\n            msg = msg.replace(body, truncated, 1)  # first occurrence in prefix area\n```\nHmm `msg.replace(body, truncated, 1)` — first occurrence. Prefix is `[TIME] [LEVEL] [name]` etc. The body could theoretically appear in prefix but no. Actually the original code does `msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\"+prefix)` using record.message. Good enough.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: record.message could be empty; len 0 <= max.\n\nCareful with keep_full_message check exactly True: `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is True`. Note `record.keep_full_message` might be 1 -> `1 is True` False. Good.\n\nTruncation math: marker = \"...<omitted>...\" length 15. remaining = max - 15. If remaining < 0? max >= 32 so remaining >= 17. head = ceil(remaining/2) = (remaining+1)//2, tail = remaining//2. For 32: remaining 17, head 9, tail 8. Matches example. \n\nValidation in __init__: keyword-only param `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None` with validation: if not None: if isinstance(bool) or not isinstance(int) or <32 -> ValueError.\n\nThe existing four positional params stay: fmt, datefmt, high_precision, use_color. Add keyword-only after.\n\n_setup_logger: pass `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Need import envs in logger. Check logger imports — need to see top of file. Let me read lines 1-32.\n\nAlso stats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nPotential circular import: environ imports? environ.py imports os, threading, collections, datetime, typing. logger imports envs — check whether environ imports logger. Not from evidence. Let's read logger head.\n\nAlso `init_logger` in logger — \"获取日志对象的函数\" required read; got it.\n\nLet me read logger 1-32 and environ class start (lines 95-130) to place config properly."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9407,"completion_tokens":1357,"total_tokens":10764,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1